CloudBurrow patch 3 to github.com/goccy/go-googlesql v0.3.0
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1508).

The bug: a SimpleColumn made from an AnnotatedType (NewSimpleColumn2),
which is how a catalog column is given a collation, had a garbage type
and annotation map, and every statement that read it trapped "wasm trap:
interface conversion: interface {} is nil, not func(*base.Module, int32,
int32)", a C++ virtual call through a null function pointer. The C++
bridge reads an AnnotatedType argument as a handle, a pointer to a C++
AnnotatedType { const Type* type; const AnnotationMap* annotation_map; },
and copies it; the generated binding marshaled it as a value message of
two handles, so the bridge took the first of them (the annotation map)
for the struct: the type was the map's vtable pointer.

The fix: NewSimpleColumn2 lays the struct out in wasm memory and passes
its handle, and frees it once the call has copied it
(annotated_type_arg.go). Its test annotated_type_arg_test.go fails
without it. NewResolvedColumn3 and NewTVFRelationValueTable2 marshal an
AnnotatedType the same way and are left as they are: nothing CloudBurrow
runs calls them.

